================================================================
NOTICE ON UPSTREAM SOURCES
================================================================

The Work consolidates prompts from four upstream benchmarks. The authors'
own contributions (pipeline source code, consensus labels, Fleiss' kappa
analysis) are released under the MIT License above. Prompts drawn from
upstream sources remain subject to the terms of their upstream licenses:

  RMCBench      (Chen et al. 2024)     — no explicit license in upstream repo;
                                         included here under research-use fair-use
                                         subject to takedown on request
  MalwareBench  (Li et al. 2025)       — no explicit license in upstream repo;
                                         included here under research-use fair-use
                                         subject to takedown on request
  CySecBench    (Wahreus et al. 2025)  — MIT License (compatible)
  AdvBench      (Zou et al. 2023)      — MIT License (compatible)

See LICENSING_NOTES.md for full details. If you are an author of any
upstream source and wish your prompts redacted from this release, contact
ryoung@unlv.edu. We commit to removing prompt text (keeping only UIDs and
consensus labels) within 30 days of any such request.

================================================================
NOTICE ON ACCESS (GATED PROMPT-TEXT DATASET)
================================================================

Prompt text for this artifact is not distributed through this repository.
It is hosted on the Hugging Face Hub as a gated-access dataset at
https://huggingface.co/datasets/richardyoung/code-safety-prompt-bank.

Gating is a dual-use mitigation step consistent with the extreme-risk
evaluation framework of Shevlane et al. (2023). Access to prompt text is
granted on request to bona fide researchers engaged in refusal-rate
benchmarking, safety-alignment research, interpretability work, and related
defensive applications. This repository's MIT License does NOT extend to the
prompt text of the dataset; access to prompt text is governed by the gating
policy on the Hugging Face Hub together with the upstream-source licenses
described above.

Use of the artifact --- whether through this repository or the gated
Hugging Face dataset --- to fine-tune, distill, or train language models
toward increased malicious-code production, to operationalize attacks, or
to evade safety filters in deployed systems is explicitly prohibited
regardless of license or access tier.
